Great 👍 this is now moving into access control per section, which is a very good design.

We’ll make it simple and scalable using SharePoint + Power Apps.


---

🎯 GOAL

Only specific users can access a section:

PR INK → King, Geryl
VP PR  → Chami, Hannah

✔ Others cannot open / answer
✔ Can be used when sending form link


---

🧩 PART 1: CREATE USER ACCESS LIST

✅ Create new SharePoint list:

SE Access List


---

Columns:

Column Name	Type

Title	(optional)
Section	Lookup → SE Section List
User	Person or Group



---

🖥️ Example Data

Section     | User
-------------------------
PR INK      | King
PR INK      | Geryl
VP PR       | Chami
VP PR       | Hannah


---

🧩 PART 2: GET CURRENT USER

In Power Apps:

User().Email


---

🧩 PART 3: CHECK ACCESS

We will check:

👉 “Is current user allowed for selected section?”


---

✅ Create a variable

In Dropdown_Section.OnChange:

Set(
    varHasAccess,
    CountRows(
        Filter(
            'SE Access List',
            Section.Id = Dropdown_Section.Selected.ID &&
            User.Email = User().Email
        )
    ) > 0
)


---

🧩 PART 4: CONTROL ACCESS


---

✅ OPTION 1: DISABLE FORM

Select your main container (form area):

DisplayMode = If(varHasAccess, DisplayMode.Edit, DisplayMode.Disabled)


---

✅ OPTION 2: SHOW MESSAGE

Insert Label:

Text = "You are not authorized for this section"
Visible = !varHasAccess


---

✅ OPTION 3: HIDE FORM

Visible = varHasAccess


---

🧩 PART 5: AUTO SELECT SECTION FROM LINK (ADVANCED)

If you send link like:

...?section=PR INK


---

In Screen1.OnVisible:

Set(
    varSectionName,
    Param("section")
);

Set(
    varSelectedSection,
    LookUp('SE Section List', Title = varSectionName)
);

Set(
    varHasAccess,
    CountRows(
        Filter(
            'SE Access List',
            Section.Id = varSelectedSection.ID &&
            User.Email = User().Email
        )
    ) > 0
)


---

Then:

Dropdown_Section.Default = varSelectedSection.Title


---

🧠 HOW IT WORKS

User opens app
   ↓
Selects section
   ↓
System checks:
   Is user in SE Access List?
      YES → allow
      NO  → block


---

🖥️ FINAL USER EXPERIENCE

Authorized:

PR INK selected
→ King opens → can answer ✅

Not authorized:

PR INK selected
→ Other user → "Not authorized" ❌


---

🚨 IMPORTANT NOTES

✔ Use User.Email (not name)
✔ Make sure SharePoint Person column is correct
✔ One row per user per section


---

🔥 PRO TIP (Better Performance)

Instead of direct filter every time:

ClearCollect(
    colAccess,
    'SE Access List'
)

Then:

Filter(
    colAccess,
    Section.Id = Dropdown_Section.Selected.ID &&
    User.Email = User().Email
)


